# Frontend

## Stack

- Server-side views with JSP.
- JSTL with `uri="http://java.sun.com/jsp/jstl/core"`.
- Reusable UI through tag files in `WEB-INF/tags`.
- Tailwind compiled through Maven.
- A dedicated theme stylesheet defines design tokens for a modern UI.
- Minimal JavaScript is used for progressive enhancement and local persistence.

## Frontend file layout

```
webapp/src/main/webapp/
|- WEB-INF/
|  |- views/
|  |  |- index.jsp
|  |  |- marketplace.jsp
|  |  |- nuevo/item-detail.jsp
|  |  `- helloworld/index.jsp
|  `- tags/
|     |- button.tag
|     |- card.tag
|     `- heading.tag
`- css/
   |- input.css
   |- main.css
   |- tailwind.css
   `- tailwind.min.css
`- js/
   `- main.js
```

## CSS and Tailwind

The build uses `tailwind-maven-plugin` in `webapp/pom.xml`.

- input: `src/main/webapp/css/input.css`
- output: `src/main/webapp/css/tailwind.css`

Use `input.css` to load Tailwind and source scanning, and use `main.css` as the
main design-system stylesheet for custom theme tokens and shared component classes.

`main.css` should be the single source of truth for semantic frontend tokens such as:

- `--color-primary`
- `--color-secondary`
- `--color-background`
- `--color-foreground`
- `--color-accent`
- `--color-muted`
- `--color-border`
- `--color-danger`
- `--color-success`
- `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`, spacing and surface tokens as needed

These tokens should be exposed in a way that works naturally with Tailwind-based
styling, for example through CSS custom properties plus shared utility/component
classes layered on top of Tailwind. Dark mode or alternate themes may also be
represented through token overrides such as `:root` and theme-specific selectors.

Prefer semantic token names over hardcoded utility colors when creating reusable
components. The goal is a modern themeable UI, not scattered one-off color choices.

## Views

JSPs live under `WEB-INF/views`, and controllers should return logical view names.
`WebConfig` automatically adds the prefix and suffix:

- `"index"` -> `/WEB-INF/views/index.jsp`
- `"marketplace"` -> `/WEB-INF/views/marketplace.jsp`
- `"helloworld/index"` -> `/WEB-INF/views/helloworld/index.jsp`

## Taglibs and links

Use the taglibs that already appear in the real views:

```jsp
<%@ taglib prefix="c" uri="http://java.sun.com/jsp/jstl/core" %>
<%@ taglib prefix="paw" tagdir="/WEB-INF/tags" %>
```

Use these additional taglibs for forms, validation, and i18n:

```jsp
<%@ taglib prefix="form" uri="http://www.springframework.org/tags/form" %>
<%@ taglib prefix="spring" uri="http://www.springframework.org/tags" %>
```

Use `<c:url>` for resources and links:

```jsp
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<c:url value='/css/tailwind.css' />" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<c:url value='/css/main.css' />" />
<script defer src="<c:url value='/js/main.js' />"></script>
<a href="<c:url value='/marketplace' />">Marketplace</a>
```

## JavaScript

JavaScript remains minimal and enhancement-oriented, and is used for a more modern
interactive UI.

Allowed uses:

- small component interactions such as dropdowns, modals, tabs, dismissible alerts,
  copy buttons, and optimistic visual feedback;
- client-side persistence of non-critical UI preferences in `localStorage`, such as
  theme, last selected tab, filters, dismissed banners, or layout preferences;
- keyboard and accessibility improvements;
- lightweight view behavior that complements, but does not replace, server rendering.

Avoid turning the frontend into a SPA. Server-rendered navigation and data flow
remain the default architecture.

## Rules

- Reuse tag files before duplicating complex markup.
- Keep JSPs under `WEB-INF/views`.
- Centralize semantic tokens and shared component styles in `main.css`.
- Abstract repeated UI into reusable components or tag files.
- Minimize repetition across JSPs, CSS, and JavaScript.
- Use minimal JavaScript for interaction and `localStorage`.
- Do not assume a SPA-style frontend architecture.
